# What `gcloud builds submit server/` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This file is mandatory, not a nicety: gcloud only auto-generates an ignore
# list when .git or .gitignore lives in the submitted directory, and server/
# has neither (the repo's .gitignore is one level up). Without it the upload is
# the whole 2.0 GB tree -- .venv alone is 1.1 GB. A .dockerignore does NOT
# filter the upload; it only applies once the context has already been sent.

.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The unstripped 978 MB checkpoint. scripts/strip_checkpoint.py produces the
# weights-only file below, which is what the image actually needs.
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/ckpt_5000.weights.pt

# Copyrighted corpus; the derived tokenizer is what ships.
data/book.pdf
data/book.txt

# Training and retraining only -- not part of the served surface. infer.py is
# excluded deliberately: it imports transformers, which is in no requirements
# file, so shipping it would put a guaranteed-broken module in the image.
train.py
train_tokenizer.py
extract_text.py
test_tokenizer.py
infer.py
tests/
inference/
requirements-dev.txt
README.md
.dockerignore
